1
00:00:14,780 --> 00:00:19,480
Those who ceaselessly hone the art
of killing are known as masters.

2
00:00:19,940 --> 00:00:24,116
These lethal abilities, dutifully
passed down through many generations,

3
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:26,917
have become what are
called modified bloodlines.

4
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,860
This is the story of one such master,

5
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:35,360
Hikaru Gero of the Poison Clan, and his
greatest challenge yet, to get married.

6
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:39,140
I hear you.

7
00:00:43,080 --> 00:00:45,080
Oh no, I slipped through my alarm!

8
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:49,151
What's the big deal, Mom?

9
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:51,517
I said to make sure I didn't oversleep.

10
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:53,718
Now I'm going to be late for school.

11
00:00:55,340 --> 00:00:56,170
I'll see ya.

12
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:00,882
If you're that eager to go to
school on your day off, be my guest.

13
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:02,380
Oh, that's right.

14
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:12,140
This is what they refer
to as a family meal.

15
00:01:12,340 --> 00:01:14,399
Just one example of human behavior.

16
00:01:15,540 --> 00:01:18,658
Next up, we have the
mixed-gender friendship exhibit.

17
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:23,217
In addition to the art of killing,

18
00:01:23,300 --> 00:01:25,837
The Gero family taught
me about the lives of the

19
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:28,626
humans I would eventually
have to assassinate.

20
00:01:30,340 --> 00:01:34,987
They lived on the other side of one-way
mirrors, unaware of what was happening.

21
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:37,480
We call it the Human Zoo.

22
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:43,220
These creatures, so fragile and
ignorant, live at the mercy of fate.

23
00:01:44,160 --> 00:01:49,440
As heir to the Poison Clan, you'll be the
one responsible for sealing that fate.

24
00:01:54,120 --> 00:01:55,557
Get a kiss.

25
00:01:55,640 --> 00:02:00,397
My life's destiny.

26
00:02:00,480 --> 00:02:02,297
The secret of the secret.

27
00:02:02,380 --> 00:02:07,137
I know you want it.

28
00:02:07,220 --> 00:02:09,137
I should love it.

29
00:02:09,220 --> 00:02:13,537
I should love it?

30
00:02:13,620 --> 00:02:14,760
Run, run, run!

31
00:02:15,660 --> 00:02:16,860
What's that run?

32
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:20,220
Fun, fun, fun! You suck! No, but, but.

33
00:02:20,900 --> 00:02:21,817
For a disruptive!

34
00:02:21,900 --> 00:02:22,730
Little.

35
00:02:22,813 --> 00:02:23,740
Thin.

36
00:02:24,660 --> 00:02:25,520
Terminus.

37
00:02:26,660 --> 00:02:27,540
False!

38
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:28,950
My. Ras.

39
00:02:29,033 --> 00:02:29,863
Mon.

40
00:02:29,946 --> 00:02:30,776
Mon.

41
00:02:30,859 --> 00:02:31,689
Muscle. Pleading.

42
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:37,020
Toxic! Audience. Puisquade.

43
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:40,230
Toxic!

44
00:02:40,313 --> 00:02:41,200
Vert.

45
00:02:50,220 --> 00:02:52,220
What do you want?

46
00:02:52,940 --> 00:02:53,770
Toxic

47
00:02:54,220 --> 00:02:55,161
I'm always here.

48
00:02:56,220 --> 00:02:57,580
I'm strange enough.

49
00:02:58,220 --> 00:02:59,050
I'm here.

50
00:02:59,133 --> 00:03:01,160
What do you want?

51
00:03:01,760 --> 00:03:03,180
Kill or kiss?

52
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:07,080
Let's go!

53
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:17,360
Kill or kiss.

54
00:03:50,220 --> 00:03:51,920
Plus, Hell's Lashes!

55
00:03:57,860 --> 00:04:02,080
My skin gives me the unique ability
to bend any fluid to my will.

56
00:04:02,660 --> 00:04:04,120
Let me demonstrate!

57
00:04:08,820 --> 00:04:09,650
No!

58
00:04:10,200 --> 00:04:13,620
Oops, did I accidentally
hit an innocent bystander?

59
00:04:13,740 --> 00:04:15,640
I'll compensate you, of course.

60
00:04:15,960 --> 00:04:18,477
Well, I would if you
were going to survive.

61
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:20,501
Pei, are you going to be alright?

62
00:04:21,340 --> 00:04:22,460
I'm confused.

63
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:24,240
Why go this far for me?

64
00:04:24,840 --> 00:04:26,120
Because it's our job.

65
00:04:26,660 --> 00:04:29,700
But in Kero's eyes, you're
more than just a client.

66
00:04:36,660 --> 00:04:39,660
But what does that mean?
Just run. Leave us.

67
00:04:41,920 --> 00:04:43,800
We only have one priority.

68
00:04:44,220 --> 00:04:45,749
Ensuring your safe escape.

69
00:04:46,180 --> 00:04:48,600
But Kero and I need a little more time.

70
00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:51,400
We'll be fine.

71
00:04:52,820 --> 00:04:55,644
Come on, tell me how I
can help you out already.

72
00:05:05,240 --> 00:05:09,380
I lost my supply of needles and
poisons after that hit. Crap.

73
00:05:11,380 --> 00:05:15,027
All that flailing is making it
impossible to get close to her.

74
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:16,340
Master Hikaru,

75
00:05:16,660 --> 00:05:21,366
you must never allow yourself to engage
a master for less than five billion yen.

76
00:05:21,540 --> 00:05:24,420
Only agree if victory is
absolutely guaranteed.

77
00:05:25,580 --> 00:05:28,557
A master must not risk exposing his arts,

78
00:05:28,640 --> 00:05:31,400
what we call modified
bloodline increments.

79
00:05:32,440 --> 00:05:34,820
Also, if someone learns your secrets,

80
00:05:35,020 --> 00:05:37,785
then you must kill them
without any hesitation.

81
00:05:38,040 --> 00:05:42,511
Their death will both preserve the
Poison Master's legacy and build upon it.

82
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:44,500
Shut up!

83
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:53,300
Special delivery for you.

84
00:05:53,460 --> 00:05:55,380
You, uh, what? For why?

85
00:05:57,060 --> 00:06:01,357
Because the Water Master would have
knocked it out of the air if I'd thrown it.

86
00:06:01,440 --> 00:06:04,146
So I dove in to make
sure it made the journey.

87
00:06:04,240 --> 00:06:05,300
I'm rescuing you!

88
00:06:05,580 --> 00:06:08,977
You should have used the opportunity
and left when you had the chance!

89
00:06:09,060 --> 00:06:10,472
Your name's Gero, right?

90
00:06:11,100 --> 00:06:12,617
I'll break this down for you.

91
00:06:12,700 --> 00:06:15,994
You think you stormed in here,
knight and shining armor?

92
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:17,339
Well, guess again.

93
00:06:17,540 --> 00:06:21,128
In case you couldn't tell, I'm
not exactly princess material.

94
00:06:21,540 --> 00:06:24,720
In short, I'm the one who's rescuing you.

95
00:06:33,340 --> 00:06:35,760
After all that, you leap into danger?

96
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:38,297
No idea what's going through your head.

97
00:06:38,380 --> 00:06:40,817
He shouldn't have bothered
with shielding you.

98
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:45,257
No doubt you're a definite shoe-in for
this year's least worth saving award.

99
00:06:45,340 --> 00:06:46,257
So tell me,

100
00:06:46,340 --> 00:06:51,105
how does it feel risking your life for an
idiot and dying for absolutely nothing?

101
00:06:52,220 --> 00:06:53,050
Kinosaki.

102
00:06:54,440 --> 00:06:56,440
Thanks for setting me up with her.

103
00:06:57,140 --> 00:06:58,740
And not someone else.

104
00:07:00,380 --> 00:07:03,180
I'm glad it was Himekawa,
and she was my first.

105
00:07:06,020 --> 00:07:08,620
Drop that syringe or the girl gets it.

106
00:07:18,740 --> 00:07:19,860
It's empty?

107
00:07:24,220 --> 00:07:26,237
Wait, I didn't see.

108
00:07:26,320 --> 00:07:29,520
How'd he sneak up behind me?

109
00:07:29,860 --> 00:07:31,840
I can't control the water.

110
00:07:47,060 --> 00:07:47,920
You're right.

111
00:07:48,260 --> 00:07:49,817
You really are a professional.

112
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:52,606
I'll call you the next
time my sink's clogged.

113
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:57,186
I've made a horrible mistake.

114
00:07:57,680 --> 00:07:59,960
Is my hand in a no-touch zone?

115
00:08:00,960 --> 00:08:02,537
Not like it was intentional.

116
00:08:02,620 --> 00:08:07,561
I basically had no choice, and it's the
back of my hand, so I don't think it counts.

117
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:08,630
Kurosaki!

118
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:09,820
What do I do?

119
00:08:32,020 --> 00:08:32,980
That rash.

120
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:35,598
You're allergic to clean air, right?

121
00:08:36,280 --> 00:08:38,157
That's why your suit's filled with water.

122
00:08:38,240 --> 00:08:40,064
To keep you from being exposed.

123
00:08:41,140 --> 00:08:43,905
I read about it in the
Poison Master's library.

124
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:47,797
I made a cream to alleviate the symptoms.

125
00:08:47,880 --> 00:08:48,821
Apply as needed.

126
00:08:49,680 --> 00:08:50,510
Huh?

127
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:52,129
And why would you do that?

128
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:54,500
Because you pity me? As if.

129
00:08:54,960 --> 00:08:57,437
I'm hammering the final
nail in your coffin.

130
00:08:57,520 --> 00:08:58,360
I beat you.

131
00:08:58,560 --> 00:08:59,678
Now I'm curing you.

132
00:08:59,960 --> 00:09:02,666
That'll teach you to
never mess with me again.

133
00:09:03,300 --> 00:09:04,476
It's not profitable.

134
00:09:04,880 --> 00:09:05,820
Losing, I mean.

135
00:09:14,120 --> 00:09:16,200
I'm sorry. Forgive me.

136
00:09:17,680 --> 00:09:20,400
I swear, I'll never, ever be bad again.

137
00:09:20,720 --> 00:09:21,740
I would hope not.

138
00:09:22,120 --> 00:09:26,355
You know, your legitimate exhibits
are pretty baller, so focus on those.

139
00:09:27,060 --> 00:09:28,300
Or will be back.

140
00:09:29,500 --> 00:09:30,400
So weak.

141
00:09:30,560 --> 00:09:31,913
Nothing but an amateur.

142
00:09:32,140 --> 00:09:35,137
You're letting him off with a
warning instead of finishing the job?

143
00:09:35,220 --> 00:09:37,477
A master kills and leaves no loose ends.

144
00:09:37,560 --> 00:09:38,390
There are no exceptions.

145
00:09:38,473 --> 00:09:42,597
If he dares to cross me again, then
he'll get my Thousand Torments toxin.

146
00:09:42,680 --> 00:09:46,798
Letting him go may seem wishy-washy
to you, but I don't kill for free.

147
00:09:47,280 --> 00:09:49,380
Is that okay with you, Himekawa?

148
00:09:50,020 --> 00:09:50,850
Sure.

149
00:09:50,933 --> 00:09:53,055
I'm never letting my guard down again.

150
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:55,760
You need a ride?

151
00:09:58,440 --> 00:10:02,852
I can't believe you didn't get it when
I introduced my shark butt, Chomsky.

152
00:10:05,440 --> 00:10:06,720
I mean, come on.

153
00:10:06,940 --> 00:10:09,017
Obviously he's a shark who's my butt.

154
00:10:09,100 --> 00:10:10,700
Isn't that right, Chomsky?

155
00:10:29,260 --> 00:10:31,600
Welcome home, Mommy! We missed you!

156
00:10:35,460 --> 00:10:38,297
Critics didn't think much
of Egg while he was alive!

157
00:10:38,380 --> 00:10:42,097
He let go of most of his
works! All of them! That is...

158
00:10:42,180 --> 00:10:44,217
Hey, why are you hiding in the corner?

159
00:10:44,300 --> 00:10:45,400
No reason not to.

160
00:10:46,140 --> 00:10:48,117
My late wife tragically passed away in a

161
00:10:48,200 --> 00:10:50,788
traffic accident shortly
after we had Akiha.

162
00:10:51,060 --> 00:10:51,890
Of course,

163
00:10:51,973 --> 00:10:53,377
we could sell the painting
and live a carefree

164
00:10:53,460 --> 00:10:55,897
life in a nice house off
the proceeds we'd make.

165
00:10:55,980 --> 00:10:56,977
But instead...

166
00:10:57,060 --> 00:10:59,117
We'd rather keep our family together.

167
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:00,920
Hey, Gero, get over here.

168
00:11:01,420 --> 00:11:04,040
Akiha wants to say thank you. I'm good.

169
00:11:04,300 --> 00:11:05,359
No need to bother.

170
00:11:05,920 --> 00:11:07,480
Cut out the lone wolf act.

171
00:11:07,660 --> 00:11:09,877
There's nothing wrong
with being appreciated.

172
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:12,372
Besides, humility just comes off as rude.

173
00:11:15,060 --> 00:11:15,890
Hiya, mister.

174
00:11:16,260 --> 00:11:19,260
I just wanted to say thank
you for rescuing my mom.

175
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:20,670
Gero,

176
00:11:20,753 --> 00:11:25,167
when I heard you were a poison master,
I figured you'd be a real piece of work.

177
00:11:25,540 --> 00:11:28,128
But I guess you're an
exception to the rule.

178
00:11:29,880 --> 00:11:31,120
My thoughts exactly.

179
00:11:31,520 --> 00:11:34,638
I was waiting for the right
time to thank you, but...

180
00:11:36,460 --> 00:11:38,060
My brother, Okto?

181
00:11:38,840 --> 00:11:41,252
He got that operation you helped pay for.

182
00:11:42,180 --> 00:11:46,945
He's still recovering, but he's got the
energy to send me dumb selfies every day.

183
00:11:47,960 --> 00:11:49,180
Can you believe it?

184
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:53,068
I tell him he's supposed to be
resting like he listens to me.

185
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:56,064
Because you're willing
to risk your life for us?

186
00:11:56,300 --> 00:11:57,260
That family?

187
00:11:57,620 --> 00:11:58,855
He may call his gang?

188
00:11:59,360 --> 00:12:02,777
And even my little brother,
they're all able to smile again.

189
00:12:02,860 --> 00:12:06,272
You do realize what you've
done is truly wonderful, right?

190
00:12:08,880 --> 00:12:10,777
Hey, where do you think you're going?

191
00:12:10,860 --> 00:12:11,690
The bathroom.

192
00:12:11,773 --> 00:12:12,617
To do some cleaning.

193
00:12:12,700 --> 00:12:13,530
For real?

194
00:12:14,060 --> 00:12:16,766
Before you go, we never
discussed your reward.

195
00:12:17,680 --> 00:12:20,957
Honestly, there aren't enough organs
between us to pay for the work you put in.

196
00:12:21,040 --> 00:12:23,517
I'd obviously love to
offer you some money,

197
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:25,697
but we're also kind of strapped for cash

198
00:12:25,780 --> 00:12:27,937
I'll give you anything
else you want though.

199
00:12:28,020 --> 00:12:28,850
Just name it

200
00:12:36,560 --> 00:12:40,160
Where the hell is Kinosaki
picking out what to wear again?

201
00:12:40,420 --> 00:12:41,832
How long does that take?

202
00:12:42,380 --> 00:12:47,700
In that case Himekawa come over and celebrate
with us three hotties out on the town.

203
00:13:06,060 --> 00:13:07,160
Something wrong?

204
00:13:09,680 --> 00:13:12,360
It's just the two of us.

205
00:13:27,420 --> 00:13:30,080
I had no clue what I
was getting myself into.

206
00:13:31,140 --> 00:13:33,600
Shark! Shark! Shark!

207
00:13:34,260 --> 00:13:35,090
My turn?

208
00:13:35,420 --> 00:13:36,250
Shark!

209
00:13:37,980 --> 00:13:40,160
Welcome to the Belly of the Beast!

210
00:13:45,320 --> 00:13:47,200
Commencing Operation Date!

211
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:52,600
Thanks to Operation White Knight,
Gato saved Himekawa from her captors.

212
00:13:52,800 --> 00:13:57,257
With his likability at an all-time high,
he managed to wrangle a date with her.

213
00:13:57,340 --> 00:13:59,928
Now tell her how you
feel and seal the deal!

214
00:14:01,400 --> 00:14:02,230
He...

215
00:14:02,313 --> 00:14:03,220
he spotted me already!

216
00:14:03,460 --> 00:14:06,872
I shouldn't have expected any
less from a master assassin!

217
00:14:10,180 --> 00:14:11,140
Remember, Gato.

218
00:14:11,420 --> 00:14:15,037
Rule number one, subsection three
of the Kinosaki School of Dating.

219
00:14:15,120 --> 00:14:17,296
If you don't know what to talk about,

220
00:14:17,380 --> 00:14:20,357
complimenting something cute she's
wearing will work every time.

221
00:14:20,440 --> 00:14:22,616
It shows you have an interest in her.

222
00:14:23,540 --> 00:14:24,500
We're in luck.

223
00:14:24,680 --> 00:14:27,033
She's covered in stuff you can bring up.

224
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:32,280
Pretty earrings, a lovely necklace,
her cute nails, or that stylish jacket.

225
00:14:33,800 --> 00:14:36,800
So, that necklace of yours. Go for it!

226
00:14:37,020 --> 00:14:38,420
It looks kind of old.

227
00:14:38,740 --> 00:14:39,860
Is it an heirloom?

228
00:14:42,880 --> 00:14:44,468
Even Himekawa's speechless.

229
00:14:45,760 --> 00:14:48,480
Uh, it came with a flea
market dehumidifier.

230
00:14:48,700 --> 00:14:50,582
Who could have seen that coming?

231
00:14:51,240 --> 00:14:53,064
That's a perfect combo starter!

232
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:55,837
A flea market dehumidifier
that came with their jewelry!

233
00:14:55,920 --> 00:14:58,038
There's tons of follow-ups for that!

234
00:14:58,580 --> 00:15:00,404
Anyway, did you cut your bangs?

235
00:15:02,780 --> 00:15:04,060
Don't give up yet!

236
00:15:04,420 --> 00:15:07,680
And look at him and Kawa,
not me! Gero, listen.

237
00:15:08,040 --> 00:15:11,177
Uh-oh, all that hard work
winning her over down the drain!

238
00:15:11,260 --> 00:15:14,142
If you're not going to
eat that, then give me it.

239
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:15,497
Thanks a lot.

240
00:15:15,580 --> 00:15:18,497
It's a good thing Himekawa's so easygoing!

241
00:15:18,580 --> 00:15:20,017
I love these.

242
00:15:20,100 --> 00:15:22,400
Did you say love? Red alert!

243
00:15:23,740 --> 00:15:25,197
This is a disaster.

244
00:15:25,280 --> 00:15:27,697
No choice, I've got to lend a hand!

245
00:15:27,780 --> 00:15:29,317
Or the state is thin.

246
00:15:29,400 --> 00:15:31,177
That must be a Greenland shark.

247
00:15:31,260 --> 00:15:33,197
Wow, you know so much.

248
00:15:33,280 --> 00:15:36,237
Oh wow, it's that support shark app.

249
00:15:36,320 --> 00:15:38,277
That they shut down due
to horrible user reviews.

250
00:15:38,360 --> 00:15:40,817
Wow, you know so much.

251
00:15:40,900 --> 00:15:43,960
It even makes whale puns! Excuse me, miss.

252
00:15:44,720 --> 00:15:45,740
That monitor.

253
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:47,697
It's off-limits for...

254
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:48,940
Even me?

255
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:51,220
What's the harm?

256
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:55,897
I couldn't help but notice
you barely touched your food.

257
00:15:55,980 --> 00:15:56,810
What's up?

258
00:15:56,893 --> 00:15:58,040
Well, actually...

259
00:15:58,820 --> 00:16:00,240
The truth is...

260
00:16:00,840 --> 00:16:03,369
I can't eat anything
someone else has made.

261
00:16:03,520 --> 00:16:05,049
It's become second nature.

262
00:16:06,180 --> 00:16:08,298
As far back as I'm able to remember,

263
00:16:08,440 --> 00:16:11,616
I've done nothing but train
to become a poison master.

264
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:16,857
As far as food's concerned, all that
matters is whether it's poisoned or not.

265
00:16:16,940 --> 00:16:20,058
I've always prepared my own
meals and ate them alone.

266
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:21,837
Sir, please!

267
00:16:21,920 --> 00:16:24,000
Show some restraint! No.

268
00:16:24,660 --> 00:16:26,601
I went through something similar.

269
00:16:28,080 --> 00:16:31,360
The entire time I was
growing up, I was also alone.

270
00:16:34,820 --> 00:16:35,800
I'm an orphan.

271
00:16:36,680 --> 00:16:40,980
I didn't have any family, and
making friends wasn't easy for me.

272
00:16:42,240 --> 00:16:46,120
And one day, a rich guy nearing
the end of his life adopted me.

273
00:16:46,780 --> 00:16:50,309
Truth be told, I think he would
have been happy with anyone.

274
00:16:51,340 --> 00:16:52,928
As the end was approaching,

275
00:16:53,140 --> 00:16:57,120
he realized he hadn't left a legacy
behind, and it terrified him.

276
00:16:57,800 --> 00:17:02,260
I inherited the Himekawa name,
not to mention a huge fortune.

277
00:17:03,320 --> 00:17:05,380
A life of luxury awaited me.

278
00:17:07,180 --> 00:17:08,460
That was...

279
00:17:10,040 --> 00:17:14,800
Until I saw the room covered floor
to ceiling with crying portraits.

280
00:17:18,720 --> 00:17:22,580
I did some digging and found out
he'd gotten them illegitimately.

281
00:17:23,080 --> 00:17:26,500
They were alone like me,
completely out of place.

282
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:31,040
And so, I returned them home.

283
00:17:33,200 --> 00:17:34,957
By the time the gallery was empty,

284
00:17:35,040 --> 00:17:38,569
the Himekawa fortune had been
eaten up from all my expenses.

285
00:17:40,040 --> 00:17:43,980
These days, I work part-time five
days a week to make ends meet.

286
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:47,529
I've got to admit, it's
kind of ridiculous.

287
00:17:49,100 --> 00:17:49,930
Hardly.

288
00:17:52,560 --> 00:17:53,390
You know,

289
00:17:53,640 --> 00:17:58,017
that job, it was the first time
someone's ever genuinely thanked me,

290
00:17:58,100 --> 00:18:00,453
and it's all because of the work you do.

291
00:18:03,200 --> 00:18:05,377
You're so dedicated. I...

292
00:18:05,460 --> 00:18:07,900
I've never met anyone like you.

293
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:22,830
Sorry.

294
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:24,412
Was it something I said?

295
00:18:25,320 --> 00:18:26,420
Yeah, kinda.

296
00:18:28,260 --> 00:18:30,731
Nobody's sung my praises like that before.

297
00:18:31,040 --> 00:18:32,569
It's sort of embarrassing.

298
00:18:45,020 --> 00:18:46,780
Don't say it.

299
00:18:53,180 --> 00:18:54,780
Shark! Shark!

300
00:19:04,520 --> 00:19:07,040
There's something I want to ask.

301
00:19:09,960 --> 00:19:13,760
You and me, how would you
feel about being friends?

302
00:19:21,980 --> 00:19:24,120
What are you thinking? Get out!

303
00:19:24,220 --> 00:19:25,691
This was your big chance!

304
00:19:29,220 --> 00:19:32,620
You had me going there.
Just friends? Sure thing.

305
00:19:32,960 --> 00:19:34,977
I thought you were going to ask me out.

306
00:19:35,060 --> 00:19:36,354
Honestly, I'd like to.

307
00:19:38,340 --> 00:19:42,046
Only, to be very blunt, I don't
know the first thing about you.

308
00:19:43,280 --> 00:19:46,280
Similarly, you don't know
the first thing about me.

309
00:19:48,040 --> 00:19:50,477
While I might have made a
good impression earlier,

310
00:19:50,560 --> 00:19:53,920
that's just how I seem on the surface.

311
00:19:55,460 --> 00:19:58,960
Deep down, there are parts
of me that are so rotten.

312
00:19:59,900 --> 00:20:01,200
I want to look away.

313
00:20:01,940 --> 00:20:04,677
I want us to share more
experiences together first,

314
00:20:04,760 --> 00:20:07,819
so little by little you can
get to know the real me.

315
00:20:08,100 --> 00:20:11,297
And then, if you still think
I'd be a good match for you,

316
00:20:11,380 --> 00:20:13,086
then I'll make that proposal.

317
00:20:16,300 --> 00:20:21,065
Since that would be the first step in
finding the happy marriage I'm looking for!

318
00:20:26,480 --> 00:20:27,717
So that's what you meant.

319
00:20:27,800 --> 00:20:29,020
I get it.

320
00:20:29,320 --> 00:20:31,849
You want this to start
off as a friendship.

321
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:35,037
You realize you just spilled
the beans on your whole plan.

322
00:20:35,120 --> 00:20:38,480
What I meant to say
was... I'm in. Be warned.

323
00:20:38,860 --> 00:20:39,780
I'm a thief.

324
00:20:40,100 --> 00:20:41,982
Stealing my heart won't be easy.

325
00:20:44,340 --> 00:20:47,164
Anyway, I figured you and
Kinosaki were a thing.

326
00:20:48,040 --> 00:20:50,720
Kinosaki is my marriage
advisor. Is that all?

327
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:02,840
Miss Himekawa!

328
00:21:04,760 --> 00:21:07,057
Since you can't eat
food other people make,

329
00:21:07,140 --> 00:21:09,980
next time, how about
you handle our lunches?

330
00:21:11,940 --> 00:21:14,058
Heads up, I'm big on rolled omelets.

331
00:21:25,820 --> 00:21:27,060
Good news, Ghetto.

332
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:30,517
You're a bodyguard now for this cutie.

333
00:21:30,600 --> 00:21:33,071
She's the only daughter of a big-time CEO.

334
00:21:33,260 --> 00:21:34,201
I couldn't dare!

335
00:21:34,320 --> 00:21:35,377
That would be cheating!

336
00:21:35,460 --> 00:21:36,937
You want me to be human scum?

337
00:21:37,020 --> 00:21:37,877
Don't be dramatic.

338
00:21:37,960 --> 00:21:39,313
You just made a friend.

339
00:21:40,300 --> 00:21:44,300
And when it comes to women, Himekawa's
the only one you really know.

340
00:21:46,140 --> 00:21:49,611
There's a great big sea out
there full of millions of fish!

341
00:21:49,820 --> 00:21:51,467
Kinds you've never heard of!

342
00:21:52,780 --> 00:21:54,997
Getting to know a lot of
girls will help you see their

343
00:21:55,080 --> 00:21:58,198
good points clearly and
learn to like them even more.

344
00:22:01,140 --> 00:22:03,457
Maybe Himekawa really is the one for you.

345
00:22:03,540 --> 00:22:06,305
Or maybe it's someone
you haven't even met yet.

346
00:22:08,640 --> 00:22:13,287
But whoever they turn out to be, I want
you to have the best marriage possible.

347
00:22:26,060 --> 00:22:27,140
Make it all

348
00:22:27,660 --> 00:22:28,490
Ah

349
00:23:02,120 --> 00:23:07,817
be creepy oh make a noise I'll be

350
00:23:28,040 --> 00:23:28,977
I want

351
00:23:29,060 --> 00:23:36,060
to

352
00:23:47,180 --> 00:23:48,160
improve myself!

353
00:23:48,400 --> 00:23:49,897
Who can cook attracts triple the ladies!

354
00:23:49,980 --> 00:23:53,320
Daigo Oshima, economics
major. My lucky stars.

355
00:23:53,700 --> 00:23:55,540
Next time, the Sound Master.
